
/*!
\mainpage

OCUDU is a complete 5G RAN solution, featuring an ORAN-native
CU/DU developed by [SRS](https://www.srs.io/).

The solution includes a complete L1/2/3 implementation with minimal external
dependencies. Portable across processor architectures, the software has been
optimized for x86 and ARM. OCUDU follows the 3GPP 5G system architecture
implementing the functional splits between distributed unit (DU) and
centralized unit (CU). The CU is further disaggregated into control plane
(CU-CP) and user-plane (CU-UP).

See the [OCUDU](https://www.ocudu.org/) for information, guides and
project news.

This is the API documentation for OCUDU, generated from the source
code by [Doxygen](https://www.doxygen.nl/). For application features, build
instructions and user guides see the [OCUDU
documentation](https://docs.srsran.com/projects/project).

Architecture notes for optional PHY acceleration are available in
\ref phy_acceleration_architecture.

Optional dApp Runtime and E3 documentation:

- \ref dapp_quickstart — end-to-end walkthrough (package, catalog, enable/disable, monitor, verify)
- \ref dapp_operations — operator and author policy
- \ref dapp_observability — metrics and copy accounting
- \ref dapp_release_provisioning — offline package signing custody
- \ref e3_management — E3 management operations and clients
- \ref e3_wire — APER wire format for E3SM-OCUDU-DAPP-MGMT-V1
- \ref e3_system_design — dApp Runtime and E3 architecture

Git-rendered Markdown index: \c docs/dapp/README.md

*/
